Hints: \(\frac{d y}{d x}=\frac{y}{x}+\tan \frac{y}{x}\)
\(\begin{aligned}
& \text { Put } \frac{y}{x}=\theta, y=\theta x \\
& \frac{d y}{d x}=\theta+\frac{x d \theta}{d x} \\
& \theta+x \cdot \frac{d \theta}{d x}=\theta+\tan \theta, \frac{d \theta}{\tan \theta}=\frac{d y}{x}
\end{aligned}\)
\(\begin{aligned}
& \int \cot \theta d \theta=\int \frac{d x}{x} \\
& \log \sin \theta=\log x+\log c \\
& \sin \theta=x . c ., \sin \frac{y}{x}=x . c \\
& x=c \cdot \sin \frac{y}{x}
\end{aligned}\)
